## CURRENT SDSC PROTECTION

The Site Diary Session Context / SDSC shadow-proof work must not be modified, discarded, staged, committed, moved or incorporated into unrelated work unless the user explicitly authorises SDSC work.

Do not mix unrelated changes into SDSC work.

## DATABASE AND INFRASTRUCTURE

Do NOT alter Supabase schema, migrations, environment variables, authentication configuration, storage configuration, DNS, Tailscale configuration or deployment configuration unless explicitly authorised.

## PROTECTED PRODUCT CONTRACTS

Do not alter an approved Zlog behaviour or design contract unless the user explicitly requests that exact change.

In particular:

- User photos must never be cropped.
- Preserve original photo aspect ratio and composition.
- Existing portrait/landscape orientation must remain correct.
- Saved diary review remains read-only unless Edit is explicitly selected.
- New Diary sticky fields must remain sticky as approved.
- Existing navigation contracts must remain intact.
- Browser/password-manager credential autofill must never itself submit Sign In or navigate into Zlog.
- Real Android phone testing is authoritative for mobile behaviour.

## SAVED DIARIES MANAGEMENT — PROTECTED BASELINE 8bd3dd3

The Android-approved Saved Diaries bulk-management UX at commit 8bd3dd3 is a protected product contract.

Do not remove, weaken, rename, or change its semantics during unrelated work.

Protected behaviour includes: compact Saved Diaries list; first-tap opens the diary; true-total count copy (never loaded/page/batch terminology); Load more diaries; Select and selection mode; Select All of the full Saved Diaries dataset via ID-only retrieval; exact-count in-app delete confirmation with an irreversible warning; MAX_DELETE_COUNT = 50 per RPC call with internal batching for larger selections; partial-batch failure handling; post-delete first-page refill; independent opened-diary Delete Diary.

Future changes to this contract require an explicit task scope and Android acceptance.

## COMMAND EXECUTION

If the user supplies an exact command:
run that exact command only.

Do not append arguments, prepend arguments, add trailers, chain extra commands, substitute another command or perform a follow-up command automatically unless explicitly authorised.

If Cursor proposes an approval command that differs from the authorised command:
DO NOT RUN IT.

## CHANGE DISCIPLINE

For every implementation task:

1. Identify the smallest authorised scope.
2. Modify only that scope.
3. Preserve all unrelated behaviour.
4. Do not stage, commit or push.
5. Report exactly what changed.
6. STOP.

Manual phone approval happens before checkpointing an accepted UI/behaviour change.

## RESPONSE DISCIPLINE

After completing authorised work, report only:

- authorised work performed
- exact files changed
- pass/fail
- blockers
- confirmation that no additional actions were taken

Then STOP.

## FAILURE MODE

When uncertain:
STOP.

Do not guess.
Do not improvise.
Do not widen scope.
Ask or report the blocker.
